[Unit]
Description=CTDI Dispatch -- production containers (dedicated slice, separate from app.slice)
Documentation=man:systemd.slice(5)

# 2026-08-06: deliberately a top-level slice (no "app-" prefix), a
# sibling of app.slice under user@1000.service -- NOT nested under it.
# systemd's slice naming is hierarchical by dash-segments: a slice named
# "app-production.slice" would be a CHILD of app.slice and would inherit
# app.slice's own memory ceiling, defeating the entire point of
# separating production from the desktop session. "production.slice" has
# no such prefix, so it lands as its own top-level slice alongside
# app.slice/session.slice/background.slice -- genuinely independent, not
# nested.
#
# 2026-08-06 (superseded 2026-08-14, see below): originally deliberately
# NO memory ceiling on this slice itself, relying only on each
# container's own Memory=/MemoryLow= pair.
#
# 2026-08-14: that no-ceiling design is what let this slice's aggregate
# usage grow unbounded even though every individual container looked
# fine on its own. Live incident: a post-reboot SWIM catch-up burst (5
# concurrent ingest.main processes) stacked with a demo backfill job --
# no single container was close to its own cap, but the SUM pushed
# system-wide swap into active churn (949MB+ and climbing, vmstat wa
# 18-29%), load average to ~6-9 on this 4-core/16GB box, and starved a
# production ops-brief generation into a 500/timeout. Individual
# per-container Memory=/MemoryLow= pairs protect containers from each
# other under reclaim pressure; nothing bounded their combined total.
#
# Sized as a matched pair with ollama.service's existing hard cap
# (MemoryMax=6100M / ~5.96GiB, MemorySwapMax=0 -- ollama.service is a
# genuine system-level unit at /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service and
# cannot be nested inside this user-level slice; cgroups don't allow a
# system unit to join a user manager's slice, different hierarchy
# entirely). Total box RAM: 16211MiB. Budget: 6100 (ollama) + 7680 (this
# slice) = 13780MiB = 85.0% of total, leaving a guaranteed 15% (~2.4GiB)
# headroom for kernel, reclaimable page cache, and app.slice, even if
# both sides hit their ceiling at the exact same moment.
#
# MemoryHigh=6656M: soft threshold -- kernel proactively reclaims from
# this slice above this point (page cache first), throttling growth
# before anything gets OOM-killed. Live-tested 2026-08-14 at a lower
# value (5632M) during the actual incident: 1-min load dropped 8.90 ->
# 6.88 and swap growth stopped dead (pinned, stopped climbing) within 5
# minutes of applying it, confirming the mechanism works as intended
# before this higher, more permanent value was chosen.
#
# MemoryMax=7680M: hard ceiling. Exceeding this OOM-kills within this
# slice specifically (production containers), never reaching over into
# ollama.service or app.slice/the interactive desktop.
#
# Cross-reference: app.slice previously carried its own memory ceiling
# (app.slice.d/50-desktop-memory-ceiling.conf, added 2026-08-06) sized
# for Claude Desktop's Electron shell plus its "Cowork" VM (up to
# 4096MB). That drop-in was removed 2026-08-14 -- Claude Desktop was
# uninstalled the same day (superseded by /remote-control), and app.slice
# now holds only lightweight infra (cloudflared, mcpo x2, gnome-keyring,
# a11y, ollama-swap-alert -- ~400MB observed). app.slice currently relies
# on systemd's baseline oomd defaults (10-oomd-per-slice-defaults.conf,
# ManagedOOMMemoryPressure=kill at 80%) rather than a custom ceiling; if
# Brave or another real desktop app becomes a regular resident again,
# revisit whether app.slice needs its own ceiling back.
#
# 2026-08-30: the 6100M "ollama" half of the budget above was never
# reclaimed when ollama.service was retired (2026-08-27 cutover to
# llama.cpp) -- corporatetraveldc-llama-hot/chat.service moved INSIDE
# this slice (Slice=production.slice in both unit files) instead of
# staying a separate system-level unit, but this slice's own ceiling
# was never widened to absorb the budget that move freed up. Root-caused
# live today: production.slice MemoryCurrent pinned at 6.93G against the
# old 6656M/7680M ceiling with 6.1G already in swap, while llama-hot and
# llama-chat -- now children of THIS slice with no ceiling of their own
# -- were the ones getting reclaimed for it (0.09-0.11 tok/s generation
# observed). The two tiers now carry their own MemoryLow/High/Max/
# SwapMax=0 (see corporatetraveldc-llama-hot/chat.service), but cgroup v2
# low/high propagation is capped by the PARENT's own ceiling regardless
# of what a child requests, so the parent had to grow too.
#
# New ceiling: same total 13780M budget the operator already approved
# 2026-08-14 (6100 ollama + 7680 production), simply consolidated into
# one slice now that there's no separate ollama.service to split it
# with. Total box RAM unchanged (16211MiB) -- same ~15% (~2.4GiB)
# headroom for kernel/page cache/app.slice as before, none of it new
# risk, just re-drawing the line between the two halves that used to be
# separate cgroup trees and now aren't.
#
# MemoryLow=6144M: new -- the old design had zero slice-level floor
# (MemoryLow=0), which Finding 1 (2026-08-29 live-state check) named
# directly: "nothing anywhere protects the resident models from being
# paged out" against EXTERNAL pressure from app.slice (the desktop
# session / claude --remote-control). Floored below the slice's
# currently-observed real (non-swapped) working set so normal internal
# reclaim among this slice's own children still functions.

[Slice]
MemoryLow=6144M
MemoryHigh=12000M
MemoryMax=13780M
